Files taken verbatim from bedrock-rs at commit d4946739^ (the commit before the
FFI sources were moved out of that repository):

  ffi/ffi.cpp         from crates/level/ffi/ffi.cpp
  ffi/ffi.h           from crates/level/ffi/ffi.h
  ffi/CMakeLists.txt  from crates/level/ffi/CMakeLists.txt

Files derived from bedrock-rs at the same commit, with changes by the ConstructCLI
authors:

  src/lib.rs   from crates/level/src/mojang/ffi.rs
               - renamed FfiStatus/FfiData/FfiResult to Status/Data/Result
               - dropped the bedrockrs_ prefix from the Rust function names,
                 keeping the C symbol names via #[link_name]
               - corrected an intra-doc link that named a function (`level_iter`)
                 that does not exist

  build.rs     from crates/level/build.rs
               - removed the `mojang-leveldb` feature gate and the git-submodule
                 fetch: in this crate the C++ sources are present unconditionally
               - link libc++ rather than libstdc++ on macOS, whose toolchain has
                 not shipped libstdc++ for years
               - pass -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration to non-MSVC
                 compilers, which current clang needs to build the vendored zlib
               - require C++14 for the CMake build, which ffi.cpp needs on
                 Apple clang

Files written by the ConstructCLI authors: Cargo.toml, README.md, NOTICE.

ffi/leveldb/ is not part of this directory. It is fetched by
scripts/setup-deps.sh and carries its own licences: Google's BSD-3-Clause for
LevelDB, and the Zlib licence for the copy of zlib built into the same target.
